<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding Garden area from a slider and using it to form and solve the quadratic</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The diagram shows a rectangular garden whose length is \({@dd@}\) metres longer than its width. Let the width be \(x\) metres.</p>
<p>Drag the slider to choose a garden, and read its area from the diagram. You will use that area in part (a).</p>
[[jsxgraph input-ref-ans0="ref_x" width="470px" height="470px"]]
var DD = {#dd#};
var brd = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-3, 17, 17, -3], keepaspectratio:true, axis:false, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false, grid:true});
var sl = brd.create('slider', [[1,-2],[13,-2],[0, 0, 10]], {name:'x', snapWidth:1, precision:0});
var wf = function(){ return Math.round(sl.Value()); };
var lf = function(){ return Math.round(sl.Value()) + DD; };
var af = function(){ return wf()*lf(); };
var p1 = brd.create('point',[0,0],{visible:false,fixed:true});
var p2 = brd.create('point',[wf,0],{visible:false,fixed:true});
var p3 = brd.create('point',[wf,lf],{visible:false,fixed:true});
var p4 = brd.create('point',[0,lf],{visible:false,fixed:true});
var poly = brd.create('polygon',[p1,p2,p3,p4],{fillColor:'#8fce8f',fillOpacity:0.5,borders:{strokeColor:'#2f6f2f',strokeWidth:2}});
brd.create('text',[function(){return wf()/2;}, -0.7, 'x'],{fixed:true,anchorX:'middle',fontSize:18,cssStyle:'font-style:italic'});
brd.create('text',[-1, 16.2, function(){ return 'area = '+af()+' m²'; }],{fixed:true,anchorX:'left',fontSize:16});
stack_jxg.bind_slider(ref_x, sl);
[[/jsxgraph]]
<div style="display:none">[[input:ans0]] [[validation:ans0]]</div>
<p><strong>a)</strong> Using the area you found from the slider, form a quadratic equation to represent the area of the garden:</p>
<div>Equation: \( \) [[input:ans1]] \( = 0 \) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><strong>b)</strong> Solve your quadratic equation to find the dimensions of the garden (in metres).</p>
<div>Width \( x = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<div>Length \( = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Whatever garden you choose, if the width is \(x\) then the length is \(x+{@dd@}\), so \[ \text{area} = x\,(x+{@dd@}). \]</p>
<p>Setting this equal to the area \(A\) you read from the slider gives \[ x(x+{@dd@}) = A \quad\Longrightarrow\quad x^2 + {@dd@}x - A = 0. \]</p>
<p>Factorising (or using the quadratic formula) gives one positive root — that is the width — and the length is \({@dd@}\) m more.</p>
<p><em>Example:</em> a width of \({@wex@}\) m gives length \({@wex+dd@}\) m and area \({@Aex@}\) m\(^2\), and \[ x^2+{@dd@}x-{@Aex@}=(x-{@wex@})(x+{@wex+dd@})=0, \] so \(x={@wex@}\) (width) and the length is \({@wex+dd@}\) m.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
